 <metadata>
  <title>nginx: Local privilege escalation via log files (low)</title>
  <reference ref_id="CVE-2016-1247" ref_url="https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2016-1247" source="CVE"/>
  <description>DOCUMENTATION: A vulnerability was discovered in nginx. An attacker who could already run commands under the nginx user id could use this access to append data to files owned by root, potentially elevating their own privileges to root. 
            STATEMENT: Red Hat Product Security has rated this issue as having Low security impact. This issue is not currently planned to be addressed in future updates. For additional information, refer to the Issue Severity Classification: https://access.redhat.com/security/updates/classification/.</description>
